<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for April 22.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for April 22.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for gas use in the period April 20 to 22.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 20 (actual) 241 mcm, 56 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 21 (forecast) 255 mcm, 60 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 22 (forecast) 248 mcm, 58 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>WEATHER:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature</p>
<p>Apr 20 (actual) 5.3 Celsius, SNT 10.1 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 21 (forecast) 6.5 Celsius, SNT 10.2 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 22 (forecast) 6.6 Celsius, SNT 10.3 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called for Monday, with none expected for Tuesday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
